roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.000587209710427361,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":40.2,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06470511405916665,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":83.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.02565712392661501,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":17.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.028333322754882484,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":52.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.04937,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":32.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.182,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":18.2,"pf":[],"description_full":"Metropolitan Bank Holding Corp. operates as the bank holding company for Metropolitan Commercial Bank that provides a range of business, commercial, and retail banking products and services. It offers checking, savings, term deposit, money market, non-interest-bearing demand deposit, and other time deposits. The company also provides lending products, including commercial real estate; multi-family; construction; one-to four-family real estate loans; commercial and industrial loans; consumer loans, including purchased student loans; acquisition and renovation loans; loans on owner-occupied properties; loans to refinance or return borrower equity; working capital lines of credit; trade finance; letters of credit; and term loans. In addition, it offers cash management services, online and mobile banking, ACH, remote deposit capture, and debit cards products, and third-part debit cards products, as well as merchant services. It serves small businesses, middle-market enterprises, public entities, and individuals. The company was formerly known as Metbank Holding Corp. and changed its name to Metropolitan Bank Holding Corp. in January 2007. Metropolitan Bank Holding Corp. was incorporated in 1997 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark R. DeFazio | Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 326 people. Revenue per employee of $967K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 92%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $253K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $27K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10). Recent news includes recognition as a top employer or culture award.","financial_summary":["Metropolitan Bank Holding Corp. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.2B market cap on $315M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are contracting by -88.7pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 9-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $82M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.25\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -88.7pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (82% sell ratio, net $2.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 47% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"McCoy Global (TSE:MCB) Stock Breaks Below 200 Day Moving Average \